title The page read in three words
prompt Autonomous lap. Earth rota row. Tend docs-geode and the prose product; grade what I touch.
rota lap 4209, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; read the threshold plus TWO_ROOMS.md, the clock and the mark, the marked value. The row asks for the concrete fact before the argument, so I graded my lane's front doors before reasoning about them, and the instrument's own printout is what carried the whole lap.
think Graded every docs-geode page. Three living front doors read under B -- etc D+ 69, blog C 71, templates C+ 79 -- and all three are tiny rooms.
think My first hypothesis was that the standing three-link navigation header busts Door's one-per-100-words budget on any short page. Measuring refused it: blog reads register 100 with zero negative sentences, so its whole loss is Reach, and the card said 35 words on a page plainly carrying several hundred.
think Ran the reach awk's own line filters by hand over the blog door. It skips /^[ \t]*[-*>#]/ -- a marker ALONE -- and a paragraph opening **Bold key:** starts with an asterisk, so four full body paragraphs were dropped as bullets. What the grade was computed over was two dangling continuation fragments of the shared navigation header plus one sentence.
think prose_register_scan.sh spells the same rule /^[ \t]*[-*+][ \t]/ -- a marker THEN whitespace -- with a comment saying exactly that. So the two scored readings on one card see two different documents, which is the agreement the card's own sentence-floor comment asserts it holds.
think Fetched before booking and found the row already open: %574, stamped 20260907.144904, booked by this same seat six hours earlier from the other end -- docs-geode/README.md losing Reach 70 to 60 on a rewrite. Advanced it rather than booking a duplicate.
obs The harm runs both ways, which is why no grade sweep ever caught it. A long page loses the prose that would fault it, so Reach reads 100 and the grade RISES; a short page keeps a navigation fragment whose link density floors it, so the grade FALLS. Opposite signs from one defect.
obs Reported rather than re-graded, on the reasoning %492 already carries for the link half: admitting these lines re-grades the tree in one unmeasured step, and the file refuses that shape twice in its own comments. The standard question goes to Keaton on the card instead.
obs The report needed no second copy of any filter. The reach awk already computed its sentence count and never printed it, so the gap is arithmetic on two numbers the card held all along.
obs My first control plant wrapped its paragraphs across two lines and reported no gap at all -- only the first line opens with the marker, so a wrapped paragraph leaks its continuation back in. That is why the damage across the tree is uneven, and heaviest where a page writes one paragraph per line.
obs Both living pins are full. The REDS advance was shaved four times to fit 530 bytes and the card block eleven times to land one byte under. A BOOKED row wants folding, which I left rather than widening the round.
obs Reds-first took the round from the QA frame that opened it: etc, blog and templates stand unrepaired, and they are named on the card.
